    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n73 Abbeyfield is a substantial four-bedroom semi-detached family home extending to approximately 150 sq.m. (1,615 sq.ft.) occupying a superb corner site of approximately 0.16 acres in one of Killester's most sought-after residential locations. Offering bright, spacious, and well-proportioned accommodation throughout, this wonderful home provides the perfect balance of living and bedroom space for growing families.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises an entrance porch leading to a welcoming hallway, a spacious living room, a large family room and a kitchen overlooking the beautifully maintained garden. A generous utility room provides excellent additional storage and functionality, while a separate plumbed storage press offers further convenience. There are four well-proportioned bedrooms, including a spacious primary bedroom with en-suite, together with a family bathroom serving the remaining bedrooms.\n\nOccupying an enviable corner position, the property enjoys mature gardens with excellent privacy and ample outdoor space, offering significant potential for further extension or development, subject to the necessary planning permission. The generous site and excellent layout make this a rare opportunity for purchasers seeking a forever home in a prime Dublin 5 location.\n\nAbbeyfield is a highly regarded and established residential development situated just moments from the vibrant village of Killester, where residents can enjoy an excellent selection of shops, cafés, restaurants, and local amenities. The property is also within easy reach of St Anne's Park and Dollymount Strand, providing superb recreational opportunities. For sporting enthusiasts, the area boasts an exceptional range of facilities including tennis, rugby, cricket, GAA, sailing, and golf, with Clontarf Golf Club, Royal Dublin Golf Club and St Anne's Golf Club all located nearby. Excellent transport links are available, with regular bus services operating along the Howth Road and Killester DART Station within walking distance, providing swift access to Dublin City Centre and beyond.\n\nViewing is highly recommended to appreciate the generous accommodation, substantial corner site, and outstanding location that this exceptional family home has to offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Porch - 1.84m x 1.70m\n\n\nEntrance Hall - \n\n\nLiving Room - 6.17m x 3.71m\n\n\nUtility Room - 4.35m x 2.20m\n\n\nStorage Press - 1.00m x 0.83m\n\n\nKitchen - 5.30m x 3.05m\n\n\nBedroom 1 - 5.27m x 2.98m\n\n\nEnsuite - 2.16m x 1.53m\n\n\nBathroom - 2.21m x 1.93m\n\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.80m x 4.27m\n\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.18m x 3.21m\n\n\nBedroom 4 - 4.61m x 3.03m\n\n\nFamily Room - 4.19m x 4.61m\n\n\n"
